<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">War of the Two Peters</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1356">1356</a>–<a href="/years/1369">1369</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The War of the Two Peters was fought between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-of-castile">Peter I of Castile</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-iv-of-aragon">Peter IV of Aragon</a> from 1356. Castilian armies repeatedly invaded Aragon and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a>, and the conflict merged with the Castilian civil war, in which Aragon backed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-of-castile">Henry of Trastámara</a>. It ended with Peter I's death at Montiel in 1369, though a final peace came only in 1375.</p></div>
